odot/labels/topic:animation","name":"topic:animation","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-02-21T19:54:38Z","updated_at":"2026-02-21T21:04:22Z","closed_at":"2026-02-21T21:04:09Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n-Reproducible in 4.6 stable and 4.4 stable\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10 - Godot v4.0.3.stable\n\n### Issue description\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8d506183-17d5-489f-bf2a-4f574cae87ef\n\nAs you can see in this video, when changing from one animation to another in blendspace, it just continues from its current frame instead of resetting to frame 1 (which would be in this case resetting to position 0,0). This also happens with frame by frame animation. Back when i was in 4.2 this wasn't an issue so not sure what the change was. Turning Sync off didn't make a difference either\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n-Open Godot 4.6\n-Create two or more animations\n-Create a blendspace1D on an animationtree\n-Set the Blend enum to Discrete\n-Move the blendspace position\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[animtest.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25460982/animtest.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com